A run of demonstrations can be costly without improving the prediction if each new pair is accepted and another request follows without analysis. After each response, record its dimensions, structural lattice/period, output shape, and exact correspondence; then test candidate mappings against all examples received so far. Dissimilar-looking examples may still reveal a common abstraction, so do not treat unfamiliar appearance as a reason to request yet another example.

